{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794520497,"nonce":"Tg94Jczoc1rhLGJF97EWhbRrUWw=","title":"A subtree rebuild lays out and measures the whole tree","message":"After the stylesheet passes were indexed (f4a6c9a), what a toggled cn switch still costs grows with the tree: 1.0 ms at 1,300 nodes, 4.9 ms at 5,200, 18.9 ms at 15,600 (debug build, style_pass_cost). A sample of the toggle loop puts nearly all of it in compute_layout, which a change to one node runs over the whole tree:\n- sync_text_measure_contexts looks at every text node (inherited_font walks the ancestors of each) when any node's font changed or a node was added; with the revision gate it only skips the layouts where nothing was.\n- compute_bounds_recursive (the visual animation bounds) walks every node.\n- taffy lays out again with the measure function run for the text nodes whose context changed, and the layout epoch moves.\n- the harness's start_all_css_animations asks every node for its animation after a layout.\n\nDirections: restrict the text sync and the visual bounds to the nodes under the rebuilt subtree and what its layout moved (taffy already caches clean subtrees); start CSS animations only for nodes that are new. Measure against the toggle loop in crates/blinc_recorder/tests/style_pass_cost.rs (STYLE_NODES, STYLE_TOGGLES).","files":null}]}